current_authority:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the current developer documentation portal for the one prelaunch TinyRustLM.com product.
  - Exactly one canonical writable TinyRustLM.com source checkout may be authoritative; ambiguity or a second writable checkout blocks all product and release work.
  - A committed change to a declared public artifact invalidates deployed-current status until a strictly newer clean-commit release passes complete readback, retired-route closure, and synchronized release records.
  - Deployment manifests and receipts are binary Git artifacts; publication fails when their byte-preservation attributes are missing or ineffective.
  - The sole current model path is the six-member SLM2 composition.
  - The default package transaction is TinyRustLM.Abstractions, TinyRustLM.Core, and TinyRustLM.P2P.
  - TinyRustLM.MemoryEndpoints is separately optional and excluded from the default transaction.

memory_endpoints_two_uses:
  direct_agent_lane: Agents working across every maintained ecosystem site use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  user_plugin_lane: A TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects its plugin as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  separation: The two lanes keep identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. Neither lane silently acts for the other.
  prelaunch_redundancy: Current .uai, wiki, public-safe notes, and approved private stores may duplicate memory for resilience only while every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.

evidence_boundary:
  - Source, configuration, fixtures, mocks, and reachability are not live memory, model, browser, P2P, or campaign evidence.
  - A publication receipt proves the site closure it names; it does not prove a qualified model or live MemoryEndpoints round.
  - Campaign counters remain 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20 until exact matching receipts exist.
  - Historical runtime material is evidence only and has no current compatibility authority.

